Subject: Interrupt-level code and IRQL under the guest CPU lock; preemption at loop edges

ISRs, DPCs and KeSynchronizeExecution routines ran on host threads beside the guest thread they
should preempt; DirectSound's voice-list relink (00582EE1) then faulted on a half-linked list.
They now take the guest CPU (waiting at most 5 ms), and DPCs wait while any thread is at or above
DISPATCH_LEVEL. A thread blocked in a wait no longer masks DPCs, and a raised thread keeps the
guest CPU across non-waiting kernel calls. A thread waiting for the guest CPU raises a yield
request that the holder honours at its next loop edge (src/fci_threads.c, tools/compile.py).
Host waits from the renderer give up the guest CPU as kernel waits do.

Its changes to src/apu/apu_core.c, from xemu, are licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later (patches/README.md).

